From: dfu-install
Subject: [PATCH] beagle: optional skip of beagle hardware probing (Nest J49)

The Nest J49 reuses the beagle target for its DFU installer bootloader,
but none of the beagle expansion hardware exists on the thermostat:
misc_init_r() probes the expansion EEPROM over I2C, drives the TWL4030
LED pins and writes beagle gpio6 bits 1/2/8/10/23 -- unknown wiring on
the J49. With CONFIG_NEST_J49_SKIP_BEAGLE_MISC=y the function is a no-op.

--- a/board/beagle/beagle/beagle.c
+++ b/board/beagle/beagle/beagle.c
@@ -248,6 +248,24 @@
  * Routine: misc_init_r
  * Description: Configure board specific parts
  */
+#if defined(CONFIG_NEST_J49_SKIP_BEAGLE_MISC)
+/*
+ * Nest J49: the beagle expansion hardware this function probes does not
+ * exist on this board (expansion EEPROM, TWL4030 LEDs, beagle gpio6 pins;
+ * see board/beagle/beagle/Kconfig).
+ */
+int misc_init_r(void)
+{
+	/* the TWL4030 power/USB-LDO setup is still needed: without it the
+	 * MUSB gadget never enumerates (no 0451:df10) */
+	twl4030_power_init();
+	/* cold boot: the PHY clock must run before MUSB does its soft reset
+	 * (a ROM USB push leaves the PHY up, a NAND boot does not) */
+	twl4030_usb_ulpi_init();
+	return 0;
+}
+#else
 int misc_init_r(void)
 {
 	struct gpio *gpio5_base = (struct gpio *)OMAP34XX_GPIO5_BASE;
@@ -442,6 +453,8 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
+#endif
+
 /*
  * Routine: set_muxconf_regs
  * Description: Setting up the configuration Mux registers specific to the
--- a/board/beagle/beagle/Kconfig
+++ b/board/beagle/beagle/Kconfig
@@ -9,4 +9,14 @@
 config SYS_CONFIG_NAME
 	default "omap3_beagle"
 
+config NEST_J49_SKIP_BEAGLE_MISC
+	bool "Skip beagle hardware probing (Nest J49 installer build)"
+	default n
+	help
+	  The Nest J49 boots the beagle target as the DFU installer's
+	  bootloader but has none of the beagle expansion hardware:
+	  misc_init_r would probe the expansion EEPROM over I2C, drive the
+	  TWL4030 LED pins and write beagle gpio6 bits 1/2/8/10/23 -- all
+	  unknown wiring on the J49. Skip it.
+
 endif
